like flowers on the ground.

259
00:14:49,600 --> 00:14:50,660
Flower hands?

260
00:14:51,080 --> 00:14:53,257
We've never grown hand flowers before!

261
00:14:53,340 --> 00:14:54,752
That sounds real creepy!

262
00:14:54,920 --> 00:14:56,280
Yeah, it must be magic.

263
00:14:56,580 --> 00:14:58,697
It's the strangest thing I've ever seen.

264
00:14:58,780 --> 00:14:59,980
They're fast, too!

265
00:15:00,420 --> 00:15:02,420
Snatched me up before I could run!

266
00:15:03,480 --> 00:15:05,300
Alright, that's something.

267
00:15:05,700 --> 00:15:09,406
They must have carried me here
after that gas made me pass out.

268
00:15:13,120 --> 00:15:15,760
I could probably use my power to escape,

269
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:19,353
and it might cause them to
panic and do something stupid.

270
00:15:23,660 --> 00:15:24,797
So, spit it out!

271
00:15:24,880 --> 00:15:26,077
What are you up to?

272
00:15:26,160 --> 00:15:29,057
You've come to destroy
our kingdom, haven't you?

273
00:15:29,140 --> 00:15:30,097
Not at all.

274
00:15:30,180 --> 00:15:33,797
I grabbed your friend, but I only
did so out of sheer curiosity.

275
00:15:33,880 --> 00:15:35,857
It doesn't matter why you did it.

276
00:15:35,940 --> 00:15:38,877
Big people are not allowed to
see the tantada for any reason,

277
00:15:38,960 --> 00:15:41,117
as the law states—you
must be put to death.

278
00:15:41,200 --> 00:15:42,177
But why?

279
00:15:42,260 --> 00:15:45,377
Whatever grudge you hold,
I have no part of it,

280
00:15:45,460 --> 00:15:47,197
and if you must keep your existence, a...

281
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:50,480
a I swear I won't tell a
soul we met! You're lying!

282
00:15:50,740 --> 00:15:52,637
I refuse to listen to your excuses!

283
00:15:52,720 --> 00:15:53,550
But I mean it!

284
00:15:55,840 --> 00:15:57,487
Okay, then, I'll let you go.

285
00:15:58,940 --> 00:15:59,770
What?

286
00:16:00,480 --> 00:16:02,480
Wow, that sure is a relief, huh?

287
00:16:02,680 --> 00:16:04,151
She's not evil after all!

288
00:16:04,320 --> 00:16:05,480
She gets to live!

289
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:09,180
That's all it took?

290
00:16:11,860 --> 00:16:13,500
You certainly are trusting.

291
00:16:14,620 --> 00:16:15,800
You can get up now.

292
00:16:17,520 --> 00:16:19,600
Here, take your sunglasses, too.

293
00:16:20,040 --> 00:16:21,000
Why, thank you.

294
00:16:22,660 --> 00:16:23,490
Hey, Leo.

295
00:16:24,160 --> 00:16:25,940
Oh, hello, Chief. Stop!

296
00:16:26,200 --> 00:16:28,560
You can't release her. Don't worry.

297
00:16:28,800 --> 00:16:30,817
She said she'll keep everything a secret.

298
00:16:30,900 --> 00:16:32,557
And why would you believe her?

299
00:16:32,640 --> 00:16:35,400
She said she means it, so it's true. What?

300
00:16:36,520 --> 00:16:38,120
Okay, then. Works for me.

301
00:16:38,400 --> 00:16:39,677
Are they all like this?

302
00:16:39,760 --> 00:16:41,642
It is rather convenient, though.

303
00:16:42,340 --> 00:16:43,520
Pardon our stares.

304
00:16:43,700 --> 00:16:46,217
It's not often we get to
see a big person close up.

305
00:16:46,300 --> 00:16:47,130
See?

306
00:16:47,213 --> 00:16:48,043
Who are you?

307
00:16:48,126 --> 00:16:49,080
The name is Gancho.

308
00:16:49,300 --> 00:16:53,257
I'm known as the Tanta Chief, which
is what we call our king around here.

309
00:16:53,340 --> 00:16:54,170
Welcome.

310
00:16:54,253 --> 00:16:56,020
You can stay as long as you like.

311
00:16:56,600 --> 00:16:57,430
Hi!

312
00:16:57,580 --> 00:16:58,580
Nice to meet you.

313
00:16:58,880 --> 00:17:01,468
Would you like to try
some simmered pumpkin?

314
00:17:01,760 --> 00:17:06,340
That's so kind of you, but I'm in a
bit of a hurry. Hey, you! Over here!

315
00:17:06,800 --> 00:17:08,624
We just baked tree sap cookies.

316
00:17:08,900 --> 00:17:10,157
You want to taste one?

317
00:17:10,240 --> 00:17:11,240
We're having tea.

318
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:12,837
You're welcome to join us.

319
00:17:12,920 --> 00:17:14,677
I'm sorry, but I really must go.

320
00:17:14,760 --> 00:17:17,280
We've got some grilled mushrooms to share.

321
00:17:18,960 --> 00:17:23,340
Excuse me, but do you know where my
transponder snail went? Right here.

322
00:17:23,680 --> 00:17:25,440
I released it into the wild.

323
00:17:28,060 --> 00:17:29,160
This is bad.

324
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:31,120
It's not long until three.

325
00:17:31,500 --> 00:17:34,340
I have to contact Law quickly. The exit.

326
00:17:35,640 --> 00:17:37,100
Where is it? Wait a sec!

327
00:17:37,340 --> 00:17:39,046
You can't be leaving already!

328
00:17:39,560 --> 00:17:40,997
And here I thought you were nice!

329
00:17:41,080 --> 00:17:43,457
If you leave, then hand over
your weapon before you go.

330
00:17:43,540 --> 00:17:44,481
That's the rule.

331
00:17:44,760 --> 00:17:46,340
I don't have one.

332
00:17:46,460 --> 00:17:48,777
Give us a weapon or we'll
take everything you've got!

333
00:17:48,860 --> 00:17:50,280
I said I don't have one!

334
00:17:56,560 --> 00:17:58,820
We're gonna bleed you dry.

335
00:18:00,260 --> 00:18:01,700
Take it all!

336
00:18:05,500 --> 00:18:07,000
No! Wait!

337
00:18:07,520 --> 00:18:08,350
Stop!

338
00:18:08,560 --> 00:18:09,960
Is there an emergency?

339
00:18:14,060 --> 00:18:16,060
You can't be mean to her!

340
00:18:16,260 --> 00:18:18,680
Her partner is a great hero!

341
00:18:19,500 --> 00:18:20,330
What?

342
00:18:20,640 --> 00:18:22,300
Huh? Hero?

343
00:18:23,040 --> 00:18:23,870
Usopp?

344
00:18:23,953 --> 00:18:25,660
But where did you hear this?

345
00:18:25,760 --> 00:18:26,660
I don't get it!

346
00:18:26,800 --> 00:18:31,100
The big person with the long nose
told me, and he said he meant it too!

347
00:18:31,420 --> 00:18:35,000
He's a legendary hero
come to save us at last!

348
00:18:36,480 --> 00:18:37,680
Finally! Finally!

349
00:18:39,960 --> 00:18:43,320
The girl came just so
we needed him most! Yay!

350
00:18:45,380 --> 00:18:46,210
Awesome!

351
00:18:46,520 --> 00:18:47,780
I want to meet him!

352
00:18:48,780 --> 00:18:50,980
Husab, what did you tell them?

353
00:18:56,960 --> 00:18:58,254
Why did you turn left?

354
00:18:58,620 --> 00:19:00,100
Put a sock in it, Tiny!

355
00:19:00,300 --> 00:19:01,476
I can't concentrate!

356
00:19:02,860 --> 00:19:03,690
Okay?

357
00:19:04,160 --> 00:19:05,720
Mom, who's he talking to?

358
00:19:06,960 --> 00:19:07,790
No one!

359
00:19:07,873 --> 00:19:08,703
Don't look at him!

360
00:19:09,960 --> 00:19:11,817
Come on, I'm in a hurry here.

361
00:19:11,900 --> 00:19:13,457
Not as much as I am.

362
00:19:13,540 --> 00:19:15,397
If I get there late?

363
00:19:15,480 --> 00:19:17,137
It's all your fault!

364
00:19:17,220 --> 00:19:19,573
Now take me to the flower field already.

365
00:19:19,960 --> 00:19:21,620
I'm going to shut up.

366
00:19:26,300 --> 00:19:28,477
Owie ow ow dang it!

367
00:19:28,560 --> 00:19:29,997
I really messed up.

368
00:19:30,080 --> 00:19:31,860
That human's gonna see me.

369
00:19:33,540 --> 00:19:34,817
Run you dummy!

370
00:19:34,900 --> 00:19:36,240
Come on hurry.

371
00:19:40,100 --> 00:19:41,140
Oh, no!

372
00:19:41,640 --> 00:19:42,720
I'm so stupid!

373
00:19:43,140 --> 00:19:45,020
I'm stupid and dumb and stupid!

374
00:19:45,340 --> 00:19:47,516
I knew I would screw this up somehow!

375
00:19:48,380 --> 00:19:50,909
You must be one of
those fairy things, huh?

376
00:19:51,180 --> 00:19:52,260
That are a toy.

377
00:19:52,500 --> 00:19:53,900
I'm not a toy at all!

378
00:19:54,100 --> 00:19:56,600
I'm Wicca and I'm from the Tonchata tribe!

379
00:19:56,840 --> 00:19:59,899
Now please promise you won't
tell anyone you saw me!

380
00:20:01,180 --> 00:20:02,220
What now?

381
00:20:03,720 --> 00:20:04,960
I can't look.

382
00:20:05,220 --> 00:20:07,817
I think I must have twisted
my ankle back there.

383
00:20:07,900 --> 00:20:09,300
I'm so dumb!

384
00:20:13,020 --> 00:20:14,560
Wow, you're strong.

385
00:20:15,020 --> 00:20:16,373
Look what you're doing.

386
00:20:16,940 --> 00:20:17,780
Please, sir.

387
00:20:18,140 --> 00:20:22,017
I need you to take me to see my
commander as quickly as possible, okay?

388
00:20:22,100 --> 00:20:25,657
I mean, this whole thing's kind of your
fault when you get right down to it.

389
00:20:25,740 --> 00:20:27,017
You stole my sword.

390
00:20:27,100 --> 00:20:28,417
What was I supposed to do?

391
00:20:28,500 --> 00:20:30,140
Stole it? Of course not.

392
00:20:30,640 --> 00:20:34,037
It's my people's job to protect
the greenery of this land.

393
00:20:34,120 --> 00:20:38,317
The big people call us fairies and give us
gifts in return for the hard work we do.

394
00:20:38,400 --> 00:20:40,165
I took the sword as a present!

395
00:20:40,340 --> 00:20:41,400
Look, I gotta go!

396
00:20:41,760 --> 00:20:43,277
I'm supposed to be scouting!

397
00:20:43,360 --> 00:20:45,537
My orders are to report to my commander on

398
00:20:45,620 --> 00:20:48,091
the whereabouts of the Don Quixote family!

399
00:20:48,920 --> 00:20:50,737
Please, we're running out of time!

400
00:20:50,820 --> 00:20:52,060
I saw them honest!

401
00:20:52,480 --> 00:20:56,097
I know for a fact they're on their way
to attack the Straw Hat's ship right now,

402
00:20:56,180 --> 00:20:57,840
so we gotta hurry! What?

403
00:20:59,540 --> 00:21:00,740
Oh, dummy!

404
00:21:00,980 --> 00:21:03,677
You just told this guy everything
you were supposed to say!

405
00:21:03,760 --> 00:21:05,937
Hey, you're not pulling my leg, right?

406
00:21:06,020 --> 00:21:07,257
I'm one of the Straw Hats!

407
00:21:07,340 --> 00:21:08,497
I really need to know!

408
00:21:08,580 --> 00:21:10,880
Ah, don't, don't, don't!

409
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:13,340
I'm so dumb!

410
00:21:13,960 --> 00:21:15,784
You're wrecking the whole town!

411
00:21:16,620 --> 00:21:17,480
Calm down.

412
00:21:17,640 --> 00:21:19,600
Once more, this is important.

413
00:21:19,860 --> 00:21:24,157
Is the Don Quixote family seriously
getting ready to attack the Sunny or not?

414
00:21:24,240 --> 00:21:28,120
I can't tell you that, but
they're not not going to do it.

415
00:21:28,580 --> 00:21:31,220
Oh, I did it again, huh?

416
00:21:33,100 --> 00:21:37,865
I don't have a transponder, Snail, so
there's no way for me to warn him about it.

417
00:21:38,500 --> 00:21:39,497
Those four, huh?

418
00:21:39,580 --> 00:21:41,160
That's not a strong team

419
00:21:43,720 --> 00:21:45,840
Alright, I'm off to the sunny

420
00:21:47,400 --> 00:21:48,230
Wait!

421
00:21:48,313 --> 00:21:49,376
Don't leave me here!

422
00:21:49,460 --> 00:21:52,617
I need you to take me back to
the flower field If you do,

423
00:21:52,700 --> 00:21:56,017
I promise I'll show you the way
back to the sea Forget about it!

424
00:21:56,100 --> 00:21:58,060
I can find my own way back

425
00:21:58,900 --> 00:21:59,730
You can?

426
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:02,118
Then why are you going your own way?

427
00:22:04,440 --> 00:22:06,160
I knew it. You're lost.

428
00:22:06,260 --> 00:22:07,613
You'll never get there.

429
00:22:10,700 --> 00:22:11,530
So,

430
00:22:11,613 --> 00:22:13,517
if those guys knew where to find us,

431
00:22:13,600 --> 00:22:17,537
they must have been following our
movements for a while now, is that right?

432
00:22:17,620 --> 00:22:18,450
Uh-huh.

433
00:22:18,533 --> 00:22:20,917
But we've been keeping a
pretty close eye on them, too.

434
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:23,882
You mean you fairies have
a beef with Doflamingo?

435
00:22:24,920 --> 00:22:25,750
That's right.

436
00:22:25,833 --> 00:22:28,940
Just forget I told you
that, okay? Damn it.

437
00:22:29,140 --> 00:22:30,217
It's not just a ship.

438
00:22:30,300 --> 00:22:31,888
The whole crew's in danger.

439
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:32,830
This is bad.

440
00:22:32,940 --> 00:22:35,420
Hey, how far is this flower field?

441
00:22:35,580 --> 00:22:37,109
Go up those stairs, there!

442
00:22:38,320 --> 00:22:40,200
I said go up the stairs!

443
00:22:42,800 --> 00:22:46,160
Well, and I thought I was stupid. Shut up!

444
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:03,860
Come back, Mr. Monkey!

445
00:23:09,500 --> 00:23:11,000
I got you!

446
00:23:19,060 --> 00:23:20,080
Keep running.

447
00:23:20,420 --> 00:23:22,067
You'll find out soon enough.

448
00:23:23,540 --> 00:23:25,300
Be wary of the police.

449
00:23:25,500 --> 00:23:27,206
You're a soldier, aren't you?

450
00:23:28,180 --> 00:23:29,010
Soldier!

451
00:23:32,160 --> 00:23:33,360
What's up, Rebecca?

452
00:23:35,740 --> 00:23:38,840
I saw the list of
competitors in the Coliseum.

453
00:23:38,980 --> 00:23:40,540
I asked you not to enter.

454
00:23:40,880 --> 00:23:42,300
Why did you do it?

455
00:23:43,460 --> 00:23:44,290
Because.

456
00:23:45,560 --> 00:23:47,840
Because I'll win. You'll see.

457
00:23:48,180 --> 00:23:49,180
I promise.

458
00:23:50,060 --> 00:23:52,580
When I do, please come back.

459
00:23:53,280 --> 00:23:55,380
I just want you to stay with me.

460
00:23:58,140 --> 00:24:00,905
If you cry so easily,
how do you expect to win?

461
00:24:01,000 --> 00:24:02,560
Come on, we need to hurry.

462
00:24:02,960 --> 00:24:05,440
Uh, are you sure? She's fine.

463
00:24:06,660 --> 00:24:07,490
Let's move.

464
00:24:18,740 --> 00:24:23,034
Brother, I don't know what's going
on, but you shouldn't make a girl cry.

465
00:24:30,500 --> 00:24:31,971
That's why we must hurry.

466
00:24:40,760 --> 00:24:44,260
I know I'm just a toy,
but I must protect her.

467
00:24:49,360 --> 00:24:53,680
These useless tin eyes of mine
can't even shed a tear for her.

468
00:25:10,740 --> 00:25:13,200
The appointed time for Caesar's handover?

469
00:25:13,860 --> 00:25:15,520
Exactly two minutes.

470
00:25:20,200 --> 00:25:21,600
Mm-hmm. Galick.

471
00:25:22,620 --> 00:25:24,457
You there, law? It's Sanji!

472
00:25:24,540 --> 00:25:25,893
Where'd you run off to?

473
00:25:26,120 --> 00:25:28,357
And please tell me you found the factory.

474
00:25:28,440 --> 00:25:30,558
That's the least of our worries now.

475
00:25:31,220 --> 00:25:33,279
You've got to get out of there now.

476
00:25:33,380 --> 00:25:34,860
We're not going anywhere.

477
00:25:35,340 --> 00:25:37,297
Handing Caesar over is part of the deal.

478
00:25:37,380 --> 00:25:41,027
Yeah, if Doflamingo actually
resigned from the seven warlords.

479
00:25:43,900 --> 00:25:44,880
As it stands,

480
00:25:45,020 --> 00:25:48,317
you're going to be handing Caesar
over for absolutely nothing in return.

481
00:25:48,400 --> 00:25:49,580
Let me spell it out.

482
00:25:50,500 --> 00:25:52,500
We walked straight into a trap.

483
00:25:52,860 --> 00:25:54,507
That doesn't make any sense.

484
00:25:55,340 --> 00:25:56,360
What do you mean?

485
00:26:07,640 --> 00:26:10,980
So the news about Doflamingo
was some kind of mistake.

486
00:26:12,260 --> 00:26:14,400
I find that hard to believe, Saka.

487
00:26:14,640 --> 00:26:16,820
The public being fooled is one thing,

488
00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:20,540
but the Navy HQ was also
duped by a false report?

489
00:26:20,760 --> 00:26:23,077
I hate to admit it, but that is the case.

490
00:26:23,160 --> 00:26:26,277
I'm headed for Marie Joie the five elders

491
00:26:26,360 --> 00:26:28,889
and I need to speak at
once on this matter.

492
00:26:28,980 --> 00:26:30,720
However, what's done is done.

493
00:26:31,440 --> 00:26:34,417
You are to continue as
planned and keep onward to

494
00:26:34,500 --> 00:26:37,560
Trafalgar law and Doe
Flamingo's rendezvous point.

495
00:26:38,580 --> 00:26:40,217
Roger that, Sokka.

496
00:26:40,300 --> 00:26:46,657
All units head to the
southeast shore, hurry up!

497
00:26:46,740 --> 00:26:49,120
Idiots, there's no time left?

498
00:26:53,160 --> 00:26:53,990
Thank you.
